// Idle Chatter (design doc: Idle Chatter, in more detail).
//
// PLACEHOLDER LINES - carried over word for word from the old Java version so behavior stays the
// same while the engine changes. They're meant to be rewritten by hand.
//
// How it plays: the game picks one "start: chatter" node by weight (each is a topic), shows its
// line, then everyone lands on "replies". Picking a tone builds Fondness - more if it's the tone
// this pony's personality likes - and the pony reacts and says goodbye.


// ---- Weather ----
// Lazy ponies talk about the weather more.

=== weather
start: chatter
weight: +3 if personality(lazy)
-> weather_storm if thundering
-> weather_rain if raining
-> weather_woods if biome(forest, dark_forest, birch_forest, flower_forest, old_growth_birch_forest)
-> weather_swamp if biome(swamp, mangrove_swamp)
-> weather_water if biome(river, beach)
-> weather_fields if biome(savanna, plains, sunflower_plains)
{pony}: Not a cloud in the sky today. Can't complain about that.
-> replies

=== weather_storm
{pony}: Some storm out there, huh? I saw a flash light up the whole sky earlier.
-> replies

=== weather_rain
{pony}: Bit of a rainy one today. Good for the crops, at least.
-> replies

=== weather_woods
{pony}: Clear skies today. The woods nearby have been quiet - almost too quiet, if you ask me.
-> replies

=== weather_swamp
{pony}: Clear day, for once - the swamp doesn't smell half as strange when the sun's out.
-> replies

=== weather_water
{pony}: Beautiful day by the falls. The water's practically sparkling.
-> replies

=== weather_fields
{pony}: Good clear day for the orchards. Can't ask for better weather than this.
-> replies


// ---- Work & craft ----

=== work
start: chatter
-> work_profession if not profession(none)
-> work_unicorn if species(unicorn)
-> work_pegasus if species(pegasus)
-> work_bat_pony if species(bat_pony)
-> work_kirin if species(kirin)
-> work_changeling if species(changeling)
{pony}: Been out plowing and hauling all morning. Good honest work.
-> replies

=== work_profession
{pony}: Keeping busy with the {profession} work, same as always.
    or: Never a dull moment being the village {profession}.
-> replies

=== work_unicorn
{pony}: Practicing a bit of spellwork when I get the chance. Still got a ways to go.
-> replies

=== work_pegasus
{pony}: Been up clearing clouds. Someone's got to keep the sky tidy.
-> replies

=== work_bat_pony
{pony}: Mostly keep to the night shift. Suits me fine - less fuss that way.
-> replies

=== work_kirin
{pony}: Just keeping to my own quiet routine today. Helps keep the temper in check.
-> replies

=== work_changeling
{pony}: Oh, you know - odd jobs here and there. Whatever needs doing.
-> replies


// ---- Village gossip ----
// Ponies with the Gossip quirk bring this up more.

=== village_gossip
start: chatter
weight: +3 if quirk(gossip)
{pony}: Did you hear? Someone's been leaving flowers on doorsteps all over the village. Nopony's owned up to it yet.
    or: Between you and me, I heard two of the neighbors had quite the argument over a fence line last week.
    or: There's a rumor going around that somepony found a whole cave of gems out past the tree line.
-> replies


// ---- Real gossip: what this pony has actually heard ----
// PLACEHOLDER lines - wiring for the gossip system (design doc: The memory system). Unlike the made-up
// rumors above, these tell real news this pony has seen or heard about another pony - each story
// once - and Gossip-quirked ponies bring it up far more. For one kind of story, branch on
// gossip(<memory type>); {gossip_subject} is who it's about, {gossip_source} who told them.

=== real_gossip
start: chatter
when: gossip
weight: 4
weight: +6 if quirk(gossip)
-> real_gossip_seen if gossip_firsthand
{pony}: Did you hear the news about {gossip_subject}? It's all anypony's talking about.
~ tell_gossip
-> replies

=== real_gossip_seen
{pony}: You'll never guess what I saw {gossip_subject} do the other day!
~ tell_gossip
-> replies


// ---- Something they've been missing ----
// PLACEHOLDER lines. The pony mentions a small wish (picked to fit them, from data/<ns>/wishes) -
// and only players who heard it can answer it with a thoughtful gift. ~ mention_wish comes first,
// so {wish} names it.

=== mention_wish
start: chatter
when: wish_to_share
weight: 2
~ mention_wish
{pony}: Ugh, I've been out of {wish} for days now. Keep meaning to get more.
    or: You know what I could really use right now? Some {wish}.
-> replies


// ---- Best friends ----
// PLACEHOLDER lines. When a friend has all three feelings high and you've lived through something
// major together, they say it themselves - once (design doc: Affection, reworked).

=== best_friend_moment
start: chatter
when: best_friend_ready
weight: 500
{pony}: Hey, {player}? I've been thinking. After everything we've been through... you're my best friend. You know that, right?
~ best_friends
-> replies


// ---- Your deeds getting around ----
// PLACEHOLDER lines. Something this pony heard about you from somepony else - mentioned once.
// Branch on gossip_about_you(<memory type>) to answer what it was.

=== gossip_about_you
start: chatter
when: gossip_about_you
weight: 6
weight: +6 if quirk(gossip)
{pony}: Word gets around, you know - I've been hearing about you!
~ tell_gossip_about_you
-> replies


// ---- Hobbies & interests ----
// Bookish ponies bring this up more.

=== hobbies
start: chatter
weight: +3 if personality(bookish)
{pony}: When I get some free time, I like to just sit and watch the clouds roll by.
    or: I've been trying to pick up a new hobby lately. Haven't quite settled on one yet.
    or: Honestly? I could talk about my hobby for hours if you let me.
-> replies


// ---- Current events ----

=== current_events
start: chatter
{pony}: Nothing much going on around the village lately - just the usual day to day.
    or: Things have been pretty quiet around here. Suits me just fine, honestly.
-> replies


// ---- Friendship & relationships ----

=== friendship
start: chatter
{pony}: It's nice having friends around the village. Makes the place feel like home.
    or: You know, a good friend makes even the dullest chores bearable.
-> replies


// ---- Cutie mark story ----
// Bookish ponies bring this up more. Changelings don't have cutie marks, so never.

=== cutie_mark
start: chatter
weight: +3 if personality(bookish)
when: not species(changeling)
{pony}: Want to hear how I got my cutie mark? It's a bit of a story, but I don't mind telling it.
    or: My cutie mark story isn't very exciting, honestly - but it means a lot to me.
-> replies


// ---- Homeland & family ----
// "present" means the relative is loaded nearby right now, so the pony can name them.

=== family
start: chatter
-> family_unknown if not family(recorded)
-> family_orphan if family(orphan)
-> family_parent if family(parent)
-> family_partner if family(partner)
{pony}: No family to speak of just yet - maybe someday.
-> replies

=== family_unknown
{pony}: Never really knew my family, to be honest. This village is home enough for me now.
-> replies

=== family_orphan
{pony}: I don't have any family of my own around here. Still, the village looks out for its own.
-> replies

=== family_parent
-> family_parent_here if present(parent)
{pony}: My family's around here somewhere, though I haven't seen them in a while.
-> replies

=== family_parent_here
{pony}: Actually, my family's right here in the village - {parent} raised me.
-> replies

=== family_partner
-> family_partner_here if present(partner)
{pony}: I've got someone special in the village, though they're not around right now.
-> replies

=== family_partner_here
{pony}: {partner} and I settled down together right here in the village.
-> replies


// ---- Breaking news you haven't heard ----
// PLACEHOLDER lines. You only feel what you know: a pony who was close to the one who died (or
// anyone, if nobody else was) tells you - once - and that's when it hits.

=== share_loss
start: chatter
tone: gentle
weight: 5000
when: news(cim:loss)
{pony}: ...Have you heard? About {news_subject}? I'm so sorry. They're gone.
~ tell_news cim:loss
-> gentle_replies


// ---- When you're grieving ----
// PLACEHOLDER lines. Ponies soften around a grieving player - even grumpy ones are gentler
// (design doc: The mood system). While you grieve, this opener takes over Idle Chatter.

=== gentle_with_you
start: chatter
tone: gentle
weight: 1000
when: player.mood(grief, clear)
-> gentle_cranky if personality(cranky)
{pony}: Hey... I heard about {mourning}. You don't have to talk about it. I just wanted you to know I'm here.
-> gentle_replies

=== gentle_cranky
{pony}: ...Look. I'm no good at this sort of thing. But about {mourning} - if you need somewhere quiet to sit, my porch is free.
-> gentle_replies

=== gentle_replies
* Friendly: Thank you.
    ~ fondness +5
    ~ trust +1
    -> gentle_goodbye
* Curious: How did you know?
    ~ fondness +5
    -> gentle_goodbye

=== gentle_goodbye
{pony}: Take care of yourself, okay? Come find me if you need anything.
-> END


// ---- Replies ----
// No pick is ever penalized; a mismatch just doesn't earn the bonus (design doc: Personality system).

=== replies
* Friendly:
    ~ fondness +5
    ~ fondness +3 if likes_tone(friendly)
    -> react_friendly
* Curious:
    ~ fondness +5
    ~ fondness +3 if likes_tone(curious)
    -> react_curious
* Bold:
    ~ fondness +5
    ~ fondness +3 if likes_tone(bold)
    -> react_bold

=== react_friendly
{pony}: Aw, that's sweet of you to say!
    or: Ha, I like you already.
-> react_matched if likes_tone(friendly)
-> goodbye

=== react_curious
{pony}: Ooh, good question - never really thought about it that way.
    or: Huh, that's actually a fair point.
-> react_matched if likes_tone(curious)
-> goodbye

=== react_bold
{pony}: Ha! Now that's the kind of talk I like to hear.
    or: Bold of you to say - I respect that.
-> react_matched if likes_tone(bold)
-> goodbye

=== react_matched
{pony}: You really get me.
    or: Feels like we're on the same wavelength.
-> goodbye

=== goodbye
{pony}: Anyway, it was nice chatting. Oh, and if you're ever looking for a gift - {favorite_gift} would make my day.
-> END
